issue_md:
### Bug Description

Javascript expression: Using ` (template literals) adds UNINTENDED SPACE after underscore if there's a fixed string before it.
The example flow below creates this output, showcasing the **buggy behaviour in the first line of the output**:

```console

- There's an unwanted space between the "chk_" and the variable-string: chk_ 123
- When I change the _ to a - the unwanted space disappears: chk-123
- When I use a variable in front of the _ instead of a fixed string, the unwanted space disappears as well: John_123

- There's an unwanted space between the "chk_" and the variable-string: chk_ 456
- When I change the _ to a - the unwanted space disappears: chk-456
- When I use a variable in front of the _ instead of a fixed string, the unwanted space disappears as well: Max_456


------------

- There's NO unwanted space between the "chk_" and the variable-string anymore when not using template literals: chk_123
- There's NO unwanted space between the "chk_" and the variable-string anymore when not using template literals: chk_456

```

### To Reproduce

Showcase flow:

```json
{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "id": "ff5abb1d-7649-4af1-ab43-a3d827566d6b",
      "name": "When clicking ‘Execute workflow’"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "08250aec-4df6-42b2-bb2f-4719774acae0",
              "name": "test",
              "value": "={{$json.people.map(person => `\n- There's an unwanted space between the \"chk_\" and the variable-string: chk_${person.id}\n- When I change the _ to a - the unwanted space disappears: chk-${person.id}\n- When I use a variable in front of the _ instead of a fixed string, the unwanted space disappears as well: ${person.first_name}_${person.id}\n`).join('')}}\n\n------------\n\n{{$json.people.map(person => \"- There's NO unwanted space between the \\\"chk_\\\" and the variable-string anymore when not using template literals: chk_\"+person.id+\"\\n\").join('')}}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        208,
        0
      ],
      "id": "62d238b3-2285-401f-8018-6fc3b555c477",
      "name": "Edit Fields"
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "When clicking ‘Execute workflow’": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Edit Fields",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "pinData": {
    "When clicking ‘Execute workflow’": [
      {
        "people": [
          {
            "id": "123",
            "first_name": "John",
            "last_name": "Doe"
          },
          {
            "id": "456",
